-# Which consequence will you keep in view after the next line arrives?
+# What survives the journey?
 
-Read one choice/exclusion pair and keep it in mind after it scrolls away. Choose a room you have walked and name one obstacle, one possible change and one observation that would tell you whether it helped.
+A change made to a body in Assembly reappears at standing scale in the final hall. The blue starting pose and amber released pose have the same thirteen joints and twelve connections. Their agreement in count does not guarantee agreement in recognition. Walk between them before asking the ledger for an account.
 
-Naming an exclusion does not repair it. Nor should every design limitation be treated as the same kind of harm. Keep the specific body, activity and consequence in view. The next iteration needs a durable record of a change and its outcome, including an outcome we did not expect. Generalisation begins when another hall presents the same relation; it remains a proposal until someone can test that second encounter.
+The encounter now has a consequence that survives unloading its source room. The ledger reports an actual saved pose. It still cannot account for the encounter that produced it: neither the movement of the visitor's hand, the reason for the alteration nor the alternatives considered are retained. A destination can survive while the way of arriving disappears.
 
-A line enters at the front; another leaves when the buffer is full. The counter survives that loss. We met a running count near the point at the beginning of the museum. Here counting and remembering separate in four lines of code. The machine can announce progress while the evidence of an earlier problem has already disappeared.
+This is a particular decision about memory. Greater numerical precision at an endpoint cannot recover a path that was never recorded. Adding a path would make another question possible, but would not establish a visitor's intention. A record's usefulness and its incompleteness coexist.
 
-The material comparison is specific: the entry count increases while old entries leave the six-line buffer. The examples are prewritten and arrive every six seconds. The display records no visitor decisions and does not save the discussion.
+The body's relations also survive. Moving a joint changes geometry without changing the graph. The name `l_hand` remains attached to the same joint even in a pose that troubles its recognition. The comparison makes an unfinished permission available to inspect: another arm would require changing the connections or the inventory, not merely another coordinate.
 
-Return to one earlier hall. Remember both an obstacle and a form you wanted to enter. Desire can locate a next experiment as clearly as a fault. The spine has supplied tools for another pass, not a final inventory of possible bodies.
+The record names no person. It can outlast a visit and be overwritten by someone else using this local installation. The empty place on a direct start and the label `LAST KEPT POSE` matter: the scene must not manufacture a past or claim ownership on a visitor's behalf.
 
-## A question the next version can test
+Desire can locate the next experiment as clearly as a fault. A form one wants to enter, a relation one wants to add, a movement one wants to remember: each gives a concrete direction for another pass through the museum. The ending offers a body to return to. It leaves open what else that body might become.
 
-Make the ledger accept a real museum observation with hall, affected activity, proposed change and later result. Preserve unresolved entries across visits. Begin with the contributor-counter ambiguity or a control whose reach has actually been tested.
-
-The earlier theoretical and design text is [preserved for further development](../../../doc/space/postcrisis-pass-2026-09-15/before/commons/maps/PostCrisis_Synthesis/critical.md). This encounter grounds the claim in the current primary artifact; it does not turn an illustrative scene into empirical evidence about people.
+[Earlier illustrative-ledger text](../../../doc/book/iterations/2026-09-21-synthesis-return/before/commons/maps/PostCrisis_Synthesis/critical.md) remains available as a baseline. The new encounter is implemented; claims about how visitors experience it still require visitors.
